'''Soul Tear''' is a [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]] that is added with the [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]] [[Skyrim:Add-ons|add-on]]. At full strength, it casts [[Skyrim:Soul Trap (effect)|soul trap]] upon foes, drains their health for 300 points on impact, and if the target is below level 100 and dies within 2 seconds, it captures their soul and [[Skyrim:Reanimate|resurrects]] the corpse to fight for you for 1 minute.
*The shout affects only the first target it impacts.
*The Reanimation works on most creatures (akin to the [[Skyrim:The_Ritual_Stone|Ritual standing stone]] effect) such as [[Skyrim:Mammoth|mammoths]] and [[Skyrim:Giant|giants]]. They abide by standard [[Skyrim:Conjuration|Conjuration]] summon rules and perks, as well as the standard one summon (two with [[Skyrim:Twin Souls|Twin Souls]]) limit. Upon death or time expiration, the thrall will crumble into a pile of ash.

Shouting one or two words will push objects a slight distance away.

== Achievements ==
One [[Skyrim:Achievements|achievement]] is unlocked when you learn all three words of this shout:
* {{achievement|Soul Tear (achievement)|descr=no}}

== Notes ==
* You can learn all three parts of the shout quickly by summoning [[Skyrim:Durnehviir (dragon)|Durnehviir]], listening to him, waiting two hours, and then repeating until all three words are learned.
* Because Soul Tear regenerates very quickly when you use the shout's first two words, it can be used to knock back opponents more frequently than [[Skyrim:Unrelenting Force|Unrelenting Force]], which has a longer cooldown for its first two words.
* Although [[Skyrim:Dragons|dragons]] are immune to being soul trapped and resurrected by this shout, the 300 health point drain will still hit them.

==Bugs==
{{Bug|The Shout may aim itself in any direction there is a living target (even behind your character), rather than the area you Shouted at, potentially killing weaker followers and angering more robust ones.|vn=1}}

